{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And now, behold, the cry of the children of Israel has come to Me.</b> Even though He said (Exodus 3:7), 'I have heard their cry,' He returned and said, 'for <b>it has come to Me</b>' — and behold, their cry has reached the Throne of My Glory, and I will not continue to pass it over to Pharaoh, because <b>Egypt oppresses them</b> beyond measure, as in the sense of 'it has reached to heaven' (II Chronicles 28:9). And by way of truth, <b>the cry of the children of Israel</b> is the Congregation of Israel, which comes to Him crying out, in the manner of 'the cry of it that has come to Me' (Genesis 18:21), and there I hinted at this." "And the sense of <b>and I have also seen the oppression</b> is to say that He will take vengeance upon Pharaoh and upon his people, because they did to them more than what was decreed upon them, with great oppression with which they oppress them, as I explained in the section 'Go forth' (Genesis 15:13)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ramban's cross-reference in Genesis 18:21 reads הכצעקתהּ (הצעקתהּ in some editions); I have rendered according to the form he quotes."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:01:44.105760892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}